### ShopEase API Tests — VS Code REST Client format
### Install the "REST Client" extension first, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### Requires the backend running: node server.js
### Tokens and IDs are automatically captured from earlier responses and reused below —
### run the requests roughly in order the first time through.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000


### TEST 1: POST /api/login — wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "customer1",
  "password": "wrong"
}


### TEST 2: POST /api/login — customer1 correct login (expect 200 + token)
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "customer1",
  "password": "demo123"
}


### TEST 3: POST /api/login — merchant1 correct login (expect 200 + token)
# @name loginMerchant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "merchant1",
  "password": "demo123"
}


### TEST 4: GET /api/products — check stock BEFORE placing an order (watch id 2, Woven tote bag)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products


### TEST 5: POST /api/orders — customer buys 2x product id 2 (expect 201)
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "items": [{ "productId": 2, "qty": 2 }]
}


### TEST 6: GET /api/products — stock AFTER the order (should be 2 less than TEST 4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products


### TEST 7: GET /api/orders — merchant sees the order just placed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 8: GET /api/inventory-risk — product with reduced stock ranks near the top
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory-risk
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 9: GET /api/kpis — totalOrders and totalRevenue reflect the order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/kpis
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 10: GET /api/orders — using CUSTOMER token on a merchant-only endpoint (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 11: POST /api/orders — ordering more than available stock (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "items": [{ "productId": 5, "qty": 999 }]
}


### TEST 12: GET /api/orders — no Authorization header at all (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders


### TEST 13: POST /api/products — merchant adds a new product (expect 201)
# @name addProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Wool beanie",
  "category": "Accessories",
  "price": 22,
  "stock": 20,
  "avgDailySales": 2,
  "icon": "🧢"
}


### TEST 14: POST /api/products — using CUSTOMER token (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "x",
  "category": "x",
  "price": 1,
  "stock": 1
}


### TEST 15: PUT /api/products/:id — merchant edits the new product's stock (expect 200, stock 50)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{addProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "stock": 50
}


### TEST 16: GET /api/revenue-summary — daily/weekly/monthly totals include the order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/revenue-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 17: POST /api/register — new customer signup (expect 201 + token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "newbie_vscode",
  "password": "testpass123",
  "name": "New Buyer"
}


### TEST 18: POST /api/register — password under 6 characters (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "shortpw_vscode",
  "password": "123",
  "name": "X"
}


### TEST 19: GET /api/insights — merchant sees Smart Advisor recommendations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/insights
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMerchant.response.body.$.token}}


### TEST 20: GET /api/my-orders — customer sees own order history (formatted as ORD-#####)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/my-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCustomer.response.body.$.token}}
